Modifications in this version
-----------------------------
This was the early, Raspberry Pi based version of the FlightTrackerLED box. The
changes layered on top of Colin's original project are:

  * Added a local Flask settings dashboard (web_interface/) so the device can
    be configured from a browser on the local network — location, tracking
    zone, brightness, altitude/ground-speed filters, weather location,
    timezone, time format, temperature units, and which plane-detail fields to
    show.
  * Added remote.it integration at the operating-system level (outside this
    repository) so units could be reached for remote support over SSH.
  * Switched live aircraft data to an authenticated (paid) Flightradar24 API
    tier. The subscription token is read from config.py / the FR24_API_TOKEN
    environment variable and is never committed (see utilities/fr24_client.py).
  * Various scene, filtering, and aircraft-naming additions.

No API keys, location data, device credentials, or other secrets are included
in this repository. See config.py.example for the placeholders you must fill in
locally.

This legacy Raspberry Pi version is different from Mach 2, which is
independently written.
